  "text": "DASHBOARD\nS1 · W6 · Regular\nGuide\nCareer ▸\n5–0\nRECORD\n+34 rd\n2nd\nLEAGUE\nAmericas\nW5\nSTREAK\n420,546 cr\nBALANCE\n86\nMORALE\n54\nCONDITION\nW6 · STAFF BRIEFING\nMATCH DAY\n\nEverything to settle before you advance the week.\n\nPLAN NEEDED\nSCOUT ELSEWHERE\n2 LOAD RISK\nMatch day briefing ▸\nTeam Nexus\n2nd · 5–0\nVS\nS1 · W6\nAMERICAS LEAGUE\nBEST OF 1\nVS ANDRE SANTOS · CUSTODIAN\nBaltic Meridian\n6th · 2–3\nTODAY'S PREP\nBaltic Meridian in W6\nSet the five, build the plan, sharpen the week.\nASSISTANT COACH\nREVIEW\nReview the suggested five\n\nApex rate among your best available options. Confirm the five and any map overrides.\n\nOpen roster ▸\nHEAD COACH\nPRIORITY\nTurn the brief into a game plan\n\nNo opponent-specific plan is set yet. Commit the tactical approach and prep edge before the match.\n\nBuild plan ▸\nANALYST\nUNASSIGNED\nPut the book on Baltic Meridian\n\nYour scout is not assigned to Baltic Meridian. Switch coverage if this match is the priority.\n\nScouting desk ▸\nPERFORMANCE\nTACTICAL\nEase the load, keep growth targeted\n\nBalance individual intensity against match readiness, then choose the team focus for the week.\n\nDevelopment plans ▸\nMATCH INTELLIGENCE\nOpponent, form, maps and run-in\n\nThey arrive on a 5-match winning run. Three points here tighten their grip on a top-four berth. Watch Voltblade — Baltic Meridian's form pick at 1.13.\n\nMAP\nBIND\nRUN-IN\nW6 Baltic Meridian\nW7 Team Vanguard\nW8 Sahara Compass\nW9 Nordic Frost\nW10 Kathmandu Apex\nBALTIC MERIDIAN — LAST 5\nL\nL\nW\nL\nW\nDANGER MEN\nVoltblade\nDUELIST\n~73\nCipherstrike\nDUELIST\n~72\nPyromark\nCONTROLLER\n~68\nMAP POOL & VETO\nBan Ascent (Baltic Meridian 100% · you 100%)\nPick Bind (you 100% · them 0%)\nAscent\n100%\n1/1\nBind\n100%\n3/3\nLotus\n100%\n1/1\nMATCH REVIEW\n\nLast time out — Beat Rust Belt Gaming 13-2. Standout: Vortex (1.59). Off-colour: Hollowlock (0.53).\n\n“Team Nexus are one of the form teams on a 5-match run.”\n\nW\nvs Rust Belt Gaming\n13–2\n★\nPOTM\nVortex\nWHAT WORKED\nPistols won\n2/2 pistol rounds (100%).\nVortex carried\nTeam-high 1.59 average rating.\nDefense is a wall\n10/12 defense rounds won (83%).\nWHERE IT BROKE DOWN\nHollowlock off-colour \n0.53 average rating across the series.\nNear their ceiling (proj. 55–66) — a lineup call.\nWHAT TO TWEAK\n▸ Hollowlock is off-colour — consider a bench or agent swap on the Roster screen.\n\nA stronger analyst would surface duel detail (FK/FD, HS%, ACS, clutches).\n\nAMERICAS LEAGUE\n#\tTEAM\tW\tL\t+/-\n1\tTeam Vanguard\t5\t0\t+40\n2\tTeam Nexus\t5\t0\t+34\n3\tRust Belt Gaming\t3\t2\t+14\n4\tSaracen Guard\t2\t3\t-1\nLAST RESULT\nW\nRust Belt Gaming\n13–2\n\nWorld #4 · Rep 62 · Fans 301K\n\nFull table ▸\nNEEDS YOU\nTEAM MOMENT\nA behind-the-scenes cut for Ghost\n\nTeam Nexus's content lead has an opening for a short video centered on Ghost. They need a direction before the crew is released.\n\nFilm the practice-room grind\nMake it playful\nSkip it this week\n▸ Vortex contract up in 3w\n▸ No game plan set for W6\n▸ 10 unread inbox messages\n▸ Coach proposed a scrim plan Match · Prep\n▸ Vortex: Season MVP Award · In Contention · 3rd · 1.49\nYOUR CALLS\nLAST MATCH\n▸ Dressed Hollowlock over the suggested five — went 0.53\n▸ Sat from the suggestion: Apex\n▸ Preparation: book on Bind\nNEWS\n[S1 W5] Vortex (Team Nexus) passes 100 kills this season.\n[S1 W5] Hollowflare (Volga Reign) passes 100 kills this season.\n[S1 W5] Riftstrike (Seoul Dynasty Prime) passes 100 kills this season.\n[S1 W5] Lunardash (Saracen Guard) passes 100 kills this season.\n[S1 W5] Grimpulse (Prairie Signal) passes 100 kills this season.\n[S1 W5] Emberwolf (Phantom Core) passes 100 kills this season.\n[S1 W5] Crimrush (Nordic Frost) passes 100 kills this season.\n[S1 W5] Ironhawk (Midnight Polders) passes 100 kills this season.\n[S1 W5] Crimdash (Lisbon Tide) passes 100 kills this season.\n[S1 W5] Voltflare (Kraken Unit) passes 100 kills this season.\n[S1 W5] Ironstrike (Ho